(DocMind AI - Field Handbook) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 689.0 Tm
(Version 2.0 | Retrieval-Augmented Generation over private documents) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 655.0 Tm
(1. PURPOSE) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 640.0 Tm
(This handbook is the reference document bundled with DocMind AI so that) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 625.0 Tm
(the system can be demonstrated immediately, without uploading a file. It) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 610.0 Tm
(is written to exercise every part of the retrieval pipeline: definitions,) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 595.0 Tm
(numbered settings, section headers, and facts that span two pages.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 561.0 Tm
(2. WHAT RETRIEVAL-AUGMENTED GENERATION IS) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 546.0 Tm
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation is a technique that grounds a language) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 531.0 Tm
(model answer in documents fetched at question time, rather than relying) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 516.0 Tm
(on the parameters the model learned during training. The retrieved text is) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 501.0 Tm
(placed into the prompt as context, and the model is instructed to answer) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 486.0 Tm
(only from that context.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 456.0 Tm
(The benefit is twofold. Answers stay current, because updating the corpus) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 441.0 Tm
(requires no retraining. Answers stay auditable, because every claim can be) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 426.0 Tm
(traced to a specific page of a specific source document.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 392.0 Tm
(3. WHY GROUNDING MATTERS) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 377.0 Tm
(A language model asked a question outside its knowledge will often produce) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 362.0 Tm
(a fluent but fabricated answer. This failure is called hallucination.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 347.0 Tm
(Grounding reduces hallucination by making the correct answer available in) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 332.0 Tm
(the prompt and by giving the system a defensible way to say it does not) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 317.0 Tm
(know when retrieval returns nothing relevant.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
