(5. THE QUERY PIPELINE) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 670.0 Tm
(5.1 HYBRID RETRIEVAL) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 655.0 Tm
(DocMind AI retrieves with two methods at once and merges the result.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 640.0 Tm
(- Dense vector search finds passages that mean the same thing as the) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 625.0 Tm
(question even when they share no vocabulary with it.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 610.0 Tm
(- BM25 keyword search finds passages containing the exact rare terms of) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 595.0 Tm
(the question, such as an identifier, an acronym, or a product name.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 565.0 Tm
(Each method fails where the other succeeds. Vector search misses exact) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 550.0 Tm
(identifiers because embeddings blur precise tokens. Keyword search misses) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 535.0 Tm
(paraphrase because it cannot match words it has never seen. Running both) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 520.0 Tm
(and combining their scores is called hybrid retrieval.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 486.0 Tm
(5.2 SCORE FUSION) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 471.0 Tm
(The system fetches three times the requested number of candidates, scores) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 456.0 Tm
(each candidate by both methods, and blends them. The default weighting is) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 441.0 Tm
(0.6 for the vector score and 0.4 for the BM25 score.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 407.0 Tm
(5.3 RELEVANCE THRESHOLD) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 392.0 Tm
(A candidate whose blended score falls below 0.50 is discarded rather than) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 377.0 Tm
(returned. This is deliberate. Returning the least-bad chunk when nothing) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 362.0 Tm
(relevant exists is what causes a grounded system to hallucinate anyway.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 347.0 Tm
(An empty result is a correct result when the corpus lacks the answer.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 313.0 Tm
(5.4 CONTEXT EXPANSION) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 298.0 Tm
(Once a chunk is selected, the chunk immediately following it is appended.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 283.0 Tm
(A retrieved passage often ends mid-argument, and the sentence that) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 268.0 Tm
(completes it lives in the next chunk.) Tj
ET
endstream
