(6. THE ANSWERING STAGE) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 674.0 Tm
(The surviving chunks are assembled into a context block and sent to the) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 659.0 Tm
(language model with an instruction to answer only from that context and to) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 644.0 Tm
(cite the page it used. The default number of chunks passed to the model is) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 629.0 Tm
(8, controlled by the setting named TOP K.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 595.0 Tm
(6.1 MULTI-HOP QUESTIONS) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 580.0 Tm
(Some questions cannot be answered by a single retrieval. A question that) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 565.0 Tm
(compares two things, or that requires one fact in order to look up a) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 550.0 Tm
(second, needs more than one pass. For these, a planner first decomposes) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 535.0 Tm
(the question into two or three focused sub-queries, each sub-query is) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 520.0 Tm
(retrieved separately, and the merged evidence is synthesised into one) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 505.0 Tm
(answer. A final verification step checks the drafted claims back against) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 490.0 Tm
(the retrieved context before the answer is shown.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 456.0 Tm
(7. EVALUATION) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 441.0 Tm
(Retrieval quality is measured, not assumed. The benchmark corpus contains) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 426.0 Tm
(1200 chunks and 60 questions with known correct answers. The metrics used) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 411.0 Tm
(are Recall at k, which asks whether the correct passage appeared at all,) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 396.0 Tm
(and Mean Reciprocal Rank, which asks how near the top it appeared.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 366.0 Tm
(Measuring both matters, because a change can improve one and damage the) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 351.0 Tm
(other. Adding candidates usually raises recall while lowering precision.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
1 0 0 1 62 317.0 Tm
(8. KNOWN LIMITATIONS) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 302.0 Tm
(- Scanned PDFs without a text layer cannot be read; no OCR is performed.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 287.0 Tm
(- Tables lose their column structure during text extraction.) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 272.0 Tm
(- Answers are only as good as the corpus; the system cannot know a fact) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 76 257.0 Tm
(that no uploaded document contains.) Tj
